  "scope": "Single local synthetic runs. Wasm capacity excludes JavaScript and sampling can miss transient peaks. Chunk counts measure received terrain packets, not verified player traversal. Nearby twenty-client runs do not establish twenty-player exploration capacity. Failed attempts retain partial measurements and are excluded from successful comparisons. Sampling ends before checkpoint/shutdown; a completed run also finishes its checkpoint.",
  "profiling_notes": [
    "Initial heap captures caused client timeouts or found a stopped world; those final dumps are excluded from gameplay comparisons.",
    "A valid nearby allocator walk identified about 5 MiB retained in generation graph edge storage and 3.49 MiB of reusable density buffers by wasm32 layouts and pointer backreferences.",
    "Several baseline and candidate attempts ended with Wrangler proxy/connection failures; the underlying cause was not established. Later probes used unique Worker names.",
    "The extra completed-stage dependency-pruning experiment was left out: the simpler selected implementation had lower observed memory use in the successful long comparison."
